; Bid only enough under points: the contract half. Winning 42 (S-0036-e,
; S-0152-c+S-0153-b, S-0153-a, S-0053-a, S-0137-e, S-0034-a, S-0033-b, S-0028-d,
; S-0128-c), with the points rule of S-0017-c. Cluster A of docs/cross-game.md.
;
; Made, a points bid scores the points taken whatever its level, so the lower bid
; loses nothing when made; set, the setters score the bid plus their points, so
; the lower bid pays less. Decided from every undecided state of the game to 250.
(dominates bid-only-enough-points
  (contracts (points 31) (points 33))
  (frame (scoring points 250))
  (utility match-win))
